# Bounce: if, paths, lets, and method calls

A ball against a wall. `if` is an expression. PlayArea is Rect, so the walls are playArea.rect.

## Schema

```
Game = PlayArea Ball
PlayArea = Rect
Rect = Int/x Int/y Int/width Int/height
Ball = Int/x Int/y Int/dx Int/dy Int/rad
```

## Construction

```
[:Game
  [:PlayArea [0 0 800 600]]
  [:Ball 100 100 -3 1 5]
]
```

## Methods

```
Rect::area = { width * height }

Ball::move = { [:Ball (x + dx) (y + dy) dx dy rad] }

Game::bounceDx = {
  r = playArea.rect.
  if ((ball.x < r.x) or (ball.x > (r.x + r.width))) { -ball.dx } else { ball.dx }
}

Game::bounceDy = {
  r = playArea.rect.
  if ((ball.y < r.y) or (ball.y > (r.y + r.height))) { -ball.dy } else { ball.dy }
}

Game::step = {
  ndx = this.bounceDx().
  ndy = this.bounceDy().
  [:Game playArea [:Ball (ball.x + ndx) (ball.y + ndy) ndx ndy ball.rad]]
}

Game::playAreaSize = { playArea.rect.area() }
```

## Target

```
%terminal

%main
public static function main():Void {
    var assemblage = GameAssemblage.factory();
    var helper = new WCHNTHelper();
    trace(assemblage.toConstruction(0, helper));
    trace("bounceDx");
    trace(assemblage.bounceDx());
    trace("bounceDy");
    trace(assemblage.bounceDy());
    trace("step");
    trace(assemblage.step().toConstruction(0, helper));
    trace("playAreaSize");
    trace(assemblage.playAreaSize());
}
```
